## Method
1. After approval, implement `scripts/sample_pca.py` and `scripts/submit.sh`. Run Python in the existing `gars-bio` environment via `_system/gars-env.sh`, using pandas, NumPy and matplotlib (noninteractive Agg backend). Check dependencies inside the scheduled job; stop if missing, without installing packages. Record package versions, resolved input paths, supplying stages and SHA-256 input hashes in the report.
2. Read the tab-separated native gene counts and CSV design. Retain `gene_id` as the identifier and exclude `gene_name` from numeric data. Require unique nonempty gene IDs and sample IDs, finite nonnegative counts, positive sample totals, and exact one-to-one sample matching to the six design rows. Reorder matrix columns to design order. Preserve fractional counts; do not round. Stop and report any validation failure; never alter upstream inputs.
3. Compute library totals across all genes. Retain genes with counts per million (CPM) >= 1 in at least 3 of 6 samples. Normalize using each sample's original library total and transform retained counts as log2(CPM + 1). Record original and retained gene counts, library totals and the threshold. Stop if fewer than two variable genes remain. This exploratory transformation accommodates the native length-scaled fractional counts.
4. Select up to 500 retained genes with the highest variance of log2(CPM + 1) across samples (sample variance, ddof=1; break ties by gene_id). Exclude zero-variance genes. Select without using treatment labels. Save selected IDs, variances and transformed values.
5. Transpose to samples x genes, center each gene across samples, and do not scale genes to unit variance. Compute PCA by NumPy's deterministic full singular-value decomposition (`numpy.linalg.svd`, full_matrices=False). Scores are U times singular values; explained variance is singular_value squared divided by (n_samples - 1), with fractions computed over all available components. Export all components and their variance fractions. Require at least two nonzero components; otherwise report the failure.
6. Plot PC1 versus PC2 with condition colors, sample ID labels, legend, and percent variance explained on both axes. Export PNG (300 dpi) and PDF. Write a concise report describing preprocessing, selected features, variance explained, and the observed treated/untreated arrangement and within-condition spread. PCA is descriptive; do not perform differential expression, significance testing, batch correction or sample exclusion. No separation is assumed in advance.
7. After successful execution, run `_system/stage03_analysis.py verify` to register the declared outputs and completion, then append its returned history entry as required by the stage contract.

